t(19, 1245, """Abu Hurayrah said: "Jibril sat with the Prophet ﷺ and looked at the sky, and there was an angel descending. Jibril said: This angel has not descended since the day he was created until this hour. When he descended he said: O Muhammad, your Lord has sent me to you: shall He make you a king-prophet, or a servant-messenger? Jibril said: Be humble before your Lord, O Muhammad. He said: Rather a servant-messenger."

And Jabir ibn Abdullah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: "Whoever says on hearing the call: O Allah, Lord of this perfect call and the prayer about to be established, grant Muhammad the Wasilah and the virtue, and raise him to the praised station You promised him, my intercession becomes due for him on the Day of Resurrection."

The Prophet ﷺ was humble, so what was the reward?

Continuing the same post on the reward given to Allah's prophet Abraham, peace be upon him, when he succeeded in the test of his son and was given the fatherhood of the prophets: here is our Prophet, our beloved and our master Muhammad ﷺ given the choice between living as a king-prophet or living as a servant-messenger, and he chose humility, so on the Day of Resurrection he was given a great station not given to any other of the messengers and prophets. For the reward is of the same kind as the deed (and the type of test).

🟢 You are tested in your patience with humiliation, so Allah raises you among people.

🟢 You are tested in your patience with harm, so Allah the Exalted makes you a master when your test ends and you succeed.

🟢 You are tested in meeting wrongdoing with kindness, so Allah the Exalted gives you honour on earth and teaches you knowledge that makes those who wronged you feel small.

🟢 You are tested in your sincerity to Allah the Exalted, so He makes the whole world obedient and compliant to you.

🟢 You are tested in your withdrawal from evil deeds and evil people until you live among people a sad stranger, so Allah gives you the company of those who are on the same path as you.

And so...""")

h(20, 250, """Our Prophet ﷺ was given the choice, and he chose!""")

t(20, 640, """In patience over the delay of offspring, many people share with Allah's prophet Abraham, peace be upon him, but what about this?

"Then when they had both submitted and he laid him on his forehead (103) We called to him: O Abraham (104) You have fulfilled the vision. Thus do We reward the doers of good (105) Indeed this was the clear trial"

Who is able?!

No one except whom Allah has chosen

And because he succeeded in what we could never succeed in, he succeeded in the test of his own flesh and blood, the reward was of the same kind as the test ..

You accepted to sacrifice the fruit of your heart .. the prophets will come from you, because the title of your obedience to Allah the Exalted was "the son"! So the prophets will be from your children!

The same kind as the subject in which man succeeds

In this is an explanation of the compensation of the Lord of the worlds in what man succeeds in by the grace of Allah the Exalted, so he continues striving against his self, does not fail, and passes the test!

🟢 Whoever strives against unlawful wealth, perhaps he will become one of the richest of the rich
🟢 And whoever strives against unlawful desires for women, perhaps he will be granted the most beautiful of wives
🟢 And whoever strives against the ego of the self, perhaps he will be granted great wisdom
🟢 And whoever strives against injustice, perhaps he will attain great elevation and empowerment on earth
🟢 And whoever strives against his own selfish share, perhaps he will attain contentment that the treasures of the earth do not equal
🟢 And whoever weeps for the oppressed, perhaps he will be empowered on earth so as to be a cause of their victory one day
🟢 And whoever weeps for the disobedient, perhaps he will be empowered one day so as to be a cause of the reform of many of them

And so""")

h(20, 2200, """Why was Allah's prophet Abraham given the fatherhood of several prophets? The greatest trial, which no creature of us could bear!""")

t(21, 255, """The journey and course of Dhul-Qarnayn in rule, in kingship and in divine empowerment on earth was never an ordinary journey, nor a model story at all! In his story are meanings hard to count for those who reflect, and in it is the grounding of many great dimensions of destiny.

It was one of the forms of divine summoning to reform the earth through a just, severe, firm ruler for a people who rebelled against the Creator!""")

h(21, 800, """The journey of Dhul-Qarnayn: summoning the just and severe ruler for reform, and for punishment too!""")

t(21, 1395, """In the Book of our Lord the Most Great, holy are His names and attributes, exalted in the heavens and on earth, high above all, there came on the tongue of al-Khidr, peace be upon him, his words to Allah's prophet Moses, peace be upon him: "And I did not do it of my own accord"

And there came the statement that the King, holy are His names and attributes, exalted in the heavens and on earth, high above all, attributed the matter of giving Dhul-Qarnayn the choice directly to the Holy Essence:
"We said: O Dhul-Qarnayn, either you punish or you take a good course with them"

Then the direct call: O Dhul-Qarnayn

Accordingly, in the Book of Allah the Exalted there were two models of receiving direct, non-legislative commands that contain no legislating of a new law, and this means that Dhul-Qarnayn and al-Khidr were neither prophets nor messengers, because what was revealed to them had nothing to do with prophethood or a message. Accordingly, the claim of any misguided person after the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ that a new religion, a new law and a new message is revealed to him cannot stand, for all of that falls by what is established by text about the seal of the messages and prophethood absolutely. The same argument is supported by what was revealed to al-Khidr and Dhul-Qarnayn, peace be upon them both, of commands of duty that in no way approach religion and legislation, which are exclusively tied to the prophets and messengers, who were sealed definitively and beyond any doubt by the message and prophethood of our Prophet ﷺ”

The words of a group of the scholars of the Salaf about the form of that revelation, different in its form, in the two models of al-Khidr and Dhul-Qarnayn, peace be upon them, are among what is used as evidence for the sealing of prophethood and all messages by the prophethood and message of the Prophet ﷺ, as they, the Salaf, explained the nature of the role of al-Khidr and Dhul-Qarnayn on earth, and that their receiving of divine commands was an exceptional human model in righteous servants who were neither messengers nor prophets. Through this door the dajjals of every age entered, especially the grave-worshipping Sufis, not the Sufis who are upon the truth, to tell their followers that they represent the model of al-Khidr, peace be upon him, and they lied. They did not dare to say that they represent the model of Dhul-Qarnayn, because he was given strong, severe kingship that al-Khidr, peace be upon him, was not given, but they mastered deceiving the minds of their followers. The verses of revelation limited to divine commands unrelated to religion and legislation are clear in the Book of our Lord about two specified persons, by the text of the Book, who are not among the prophets and messengers, and we hold as our creed what the text in the Book of our Lord the Most Great says. Based on that, everyone who claims that a revelation of deeds and duty comes to him is a dajjal, unless that is proven by an overpowering, irrefutable authority from Allah the Exalted, which can never be achieved except through heavenly and earthly signs supported by Allah the Exalted, overpowering and dominant, from which together result the might of the religion and the faith, the rise of the Ummah, the death of the fitnah and the presence of Allah's command on earth. This is among the certain unseen whose truth only Allah the Exalted knows, and the talk here is for understanding, not for affirming the inevitability of the two models of al-Khidr and Dhul-Qarnayn occurring at the end of time, because it is unseen that should not be foreseen by understanding or by ijtihad. With this the falsehoods of the dajjals of all ages fall.""")

h(22, 400, """Dhul-Qarnayn and al-Khidr: the two exceptions for a profound divine wisdom""")

t(22, 1000, """Dhul-Qarnayn was guided, set right, granted success, sound in opinion, wise, just and not tyrannical, and he understood the interests of the servants and what was good for them. That is why he was given complete and overpowering empowerment on earth, not limited empowerment, and then he was given a choice in what he would do, and this choice was directly from the Lord Most Great. It is established from Imam Ali, peace be upon him, with an authentic chain, that he said Dhul-Qarnayn was neither a prophet nor a messenger of the prophets and messengers of Allah the Exalted.

So we are before a model higher in empowerment than al-Khidr, and they are two models of two righteous servants who reached a very high level of relationship with Allah the Exalted, and this is so that we understand that our relationship with Allah the Exalted is open and has no limits. As for choosing being a truth, yes; even among non-prophets there are those chosen for roles that may seem earthly to people but are in reality heavenly. Qutuz, Saladin, Ertugrul and others among the models of building are chosen by appointment for roles before their creation, and yet this never prevents the truth of the wider, more comprehensive and more general choosings of servanthood among people without specification.

Our Lord the Most Great, holy are His names, exalted in the heavens and on earth, high above all, said about Dhul-Qarnayn:

“Until, when he reached the setting of the sun, he found it setting in a spring of dark mud, and he found near it a people. We said: O Dhul-Qarnayn, either you punish or you take a good course with them * He said: As for one who wrongs, we will punish him, then he will be returned to his Lord, and He will punish him with a terrible punishment * But as for one who believes and does righteousness, he will have a reward of the best, and we will speak to him from our command with ease”""")

h(22, 2000, """When Dhul-Qarnayn found a disobedient people on his way, Allah gave him absolute rule over them!""")

h(23, 350, """Dhul-Qarnayn went around the earth setting it right, and the Dajjal will go around it destroying""")

t(23, 920, """Its finality as a religion: one of the reasons for it is the comprehensiveness of its building as a legislation.

In the first establishment of its political body in Madinah, in the first moments of the Hijrah, the Prophet ﷺ set up 3 sovereign ministries in our modern understanding:
🔴 Ministry of finance
🔴 Ministry of the interior
🔴 Ministry of foreign affairs

Any project of reform on earth or project of liberation, and I gave Vietnam earlier as a modern example, can never move a single stone on earth without:
🔴 Money
🔴 Internal strength
🔴 Regional or international political relations

The first regional relations covered by the lawful prophetic policy were the agreements with the powers surrounding the body of Madinah al-Munawwarah, and they were political and internal security agreements. Then the noble prophetic state established its financial legislation and its resources. Thus we find that even the divine project (religion and monotheism) does not stand without money, without international political alignments and without internal security. If any reform project loses these three elements, it stumbles, weakens or is erased!""")

