t(24, 1375, """Sensory competence is of the mind, not of the limbs .. The psychological factor is decisive and central in our perception of things; the original perceiver is the mind, not the hand, the foot or the eye. Perceptions in themselves have an amazing variety and instantaneous alignment that shows the greatness of Allah the Exalted's creation in us, because our souls are a very great creation, not a simple one.. One day, in the experience of fearing to be late for the Friday sermon, I crossed a street that was truly, not relatively, long, tense and fearing to be late for the mosque, and I felt that the street was very long and that the time I spent reaching the mosque was a very long time. When the sermon and prayer ended and we left the mosque, on the way back home the same street I had crossed was not long at all as it had felt on the way there, and the effort on the way back did not equal even 10% of the effort imagined to be great on the way there!

So you do not see identical things in your life; rather your life is a mosaic of disordered, inconsistent feelings. Factors of weather and climate, positive and negative desire in you or in those around you, sound and wrong beliefs, inherited ideas, immediate personal goals, medium and long term personal goals, the influences of environment and surroundings, and dozens of other overlapping things, all make your changing feeling toward things, matters and situations, and all contribute in one way or another to your knowledge structure, your abstract intellectual structure, or your acquired copying structure. So humanity lived and will die without perceiving almost anything that could be called decisive about the truths of the human soul and the greatness of its creation, except what our Lord the Most Great taught us in His Book.""")

h(24, 2300, """Awareness = the limbs. A street you cross tense is very long, and the same one you cross calm is very short!""")

