t(26, 1160, """If I were given the treasures of the easts and the wests to break a confining destiny, I would not do it unless Allah lifted the confinement of the destiny by His power, because every destiny that confines you from its opposite is good, just as every destiny is pure good .. If you are certain that the kind of destiny is one that confines you from its opposite, know that the confinement is a Yunus-like confinement. So beware of striving unless your destiny changes without your own planning, because then it would be punishment and wrath from the Lord Most Great, followed by a ruin after which there is no salvation, or a ruin that melts flesh, bone and soul before mercy descends. Whoever grasps the lesson of Yunus is saved, Allah willing.""")

